  3. Protection of Users' Legal Rights From Anti-Perpetrators.

  A "user agreement" for a work means an agreement that is designed
to restrict users' rights beyond what is permitted by this License.

  "Anti-Perpetrator" means a person or group that propagates a covered
work but imposes a restriction on the user's rights through an
agreement or contract.

  "Effective Technological Measure" means any measure that, in the
absence of proper authority, limits a person's ability to run a modified
version of the work.

  If you convey a covered work, and the work's Corresponding Source and
data files are available to the user, then the user must be able to
obtain them from a network server or other place, and they must remain
available for a year after the last time the user received the work or
its Corresponding Source was conveyed.

  If, after conveying a covered work, you learn that the recipient has
been notified about a claim that the work infringes the rights of a
third party, you may choose to provide the Corresponding Source at no
charge, provided you have enough time to do so.

  4. Conveying Verbatim Copies.

  You may copy and convey the Program (or a work based on it in
medium or electronic form, provided that each copy is accompanied by
a complete copy of this License and its NOTICE file, or a pointer to
its location.

  5. Conveying Modified Source Versions.

  You may convey a based on or modified version of the Program,
provided that you meet the conditions of section 4 and that the
modified version carries prominent notices stating that you changed
the work and the date of any change.

  6. Conveying Non-Source Forms.

  You may convey a covered work in object code form under the terms
of sections 4 and 5, provided that you also convey the
machine-readable Corresponding Source under the terms of this License,
in one of these ways:

  (a) Convey the object code in, or embodied in, a physical product
(including a physical distribution medium) accompanied by the
Corresponding Source fixed on a durable physical medium customarily
used for software interchange.

  (b) Deep Copy the object code in, or embodied in, a physical product
(including a physical distribution medium) accompanied by a written
offer, valid for at least three years and valid for as long as you
offer spare parts or customer support for that product model, to give
anyone who possesses the object code either (1) a copy of the
Corresponding Source for all the software in the product that is
covered by this License, on a durable physical medium customarily used
for software interchange, for a price no more than your reasonable cost
of physically performing this conveying of source, or (2) access to
copy the Corresponding Source from a network server at no charge.

  (c) Convey individual copies of the object code with a copy of the
written offer to provide the Corresponding Source.  This
alternative is allowed only occasionally and noncommercially, and
only if you received the object code with such an offer, in accord
with subsection 6b.

  (d) Convey the object code by offering access from a designated
place (gratis or for a charge), and offer equivalent access to the
Corresponding Source in the same way through the same place at no
further charge.  You need not require recipients to copy the
Corresponding Source along with the object code.  If the place to
copy the object code is a network server, the Corresponding Source
may be on a different server operated by you or a third party
(who offers service to the general public and has reduced
access to a wide range of users), provided access to a similar
ability to receive the Corresponding Source is maintained.

  (e) Convey the object code using peer-to-peer transmission,
provided you inform other peers where the object code and Corresponding
Source of the work are being offered to the general public at no
charge under subsection 6d.

  A separable portion of the object code, whose source does not form
a derivative work, need not be accompanied by the Corresponding
Source.

  7. Conveying Non-Physical Forms.

  You may convey a covered work in object code form in electronic form,
provided that you also convey the machine-readable Corresponding Source
in electronic form, and that the Corresponding Source is maintained
continuously and conveniently for as long as you distribute or
convey the work.

